help_exec() {
    cat <<EOF
$PROG exec [options] [--] COMMAND [ARGUMENT ...]

Run a command in every repository, several at a time, and print what it
wrote under the name of each repository, in the order of the folders. The
command starts at "--", or at the first word that is not an option, and
keeps the rest of the line. It runs in the top folder of the repository,
without a terminal, with GH_BATCH_REPO (the path) and GH_BATCH_NAME (the
name) in its environment. A repository where it wrote nothing and succeeded
is only counted.

  $PROG exec git gc --quiet
  $PROG exec --dirty -- git diff --stat
  $PROG exec --in ~/papers -- sh -c 'ls *.tex 2>/dev/null | wc -l'

OPTIONS
      --in DIR       a folder to search, or a name, repeatable (neither can
                     be a plain word here: the command starts there)
      --dirty        only the repositories with pending changes
      --clean        only those without
      --ahead        only those with commits to push
      --behind       only those behind the last fetch
      --timeout SEC  stop a command that runs longer (default: no limit)
  and the common options, see: $PROG help

The exit status is 1 when the command failed somewhere.
EOF
}

help_doctor() {
    cat <<EOF
$PROG doctor [options] [folder or name ...]

Health check. Nothing is changed. For each repository:

  problems   an operation left in progress, unresolved conflicts, a branch
             whose upstream is gone, a password or a token written in the
             address of a remote, a repository that GitHub does not know,
             a folder that git refuses to read
  warnings   no remote (the repository exists on this machine only), a
             detached HEAD, a branch that follows nothing, pending changes
             or unpushed commits older than a week, stashes, a remote that
             was renamed or transferred on GitHub (with the command that
             corrects its address), an archived repository, git-lfs needed
             and missing, backups and kept files of this tool older than
             a week (a note while they are recent)

And around the repositories: the folders of the workspace that hold no
